  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#2686\", \"PowerToys#35975\", \"PowerToys#33148\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#2686 is the main tracking issue for adding an output-format option to Image Resizer. Commenters there ask for HEIC→JPG and PNG→JPG, among other formats. PowerToys#35975 and #33148 asked for the same HEIC→JPG-while-resizing option, and #35975 was closed as a duplicate of #2686. Image Resizer currently keeps the original file format, and the archive shows no released fix. Add a 👍 reaction to #2686 and your scenario there instead of filing a new issue. In the meantime, convert the HEIC files to JPG with another tool, then resize them. Related requests for a general converter are #36807 and #35796. A new HEIC→JPG/PNG conversion request is #48206, which asks for it through Advanced Paste.\"}",
